\paragraph{Codebook variant.}
The runs of \cref{tab:v2} use the hidden-token energy model of \cref{app:pilot} with the answer
codebook on the visible tokens ($\kappa_{\mathrm{ans}}=0.5$, $\beta_{\mathrm{ans}}=\sqrt d$ at the
end of the schedule, prototypes initialized as orthonormal directions and kept at unit norm), the
tied readout with a learned scale, the digit embedding tied to the prototypes, the $\beta$ schedule
$\rho=8$ over the first $K=8$ iterations applied to both memory terms (so the energy is only
non-increasing after iteration $8$, and the energy-increase counter of \cref{app:pilot} is not
meaningful during the schedule), the ranking loss with weight $0.1$, margin $1$ and $R=2$ restarts
per puzzle (batch $64\times2$), and otherwise the training recipe of \cref{app:pilot}; $2{,}000$
steps on $4\times4$ and $4{,}000$ on $6\times6$. The memory-MLP ablation of SFPRM uses $256$ tied
memories with a learned $\beta$ in place of the GELU MLP in both nGPT layers. Evaluation adds a third
halting rule, Armijo backtracking with the commitment requirement, and reports the commitment
statistics at the Armijo-halted state. \Cref{fig:v2} shows the training curves, halting
distributions, spectra and restart curves of the full codebook variant against SFPRM. V2APP

